## Pin: `Task.spawn_raw` ownership-move (closes
## project_ruxen_task_spawn_ownership_gap.md).
##
## `library/std/future/runtime/scheduler.c:150-152` documents that
## `Task.spawn_raw(future)` takes ownership of the future heap
## block — the caller's binding falls out of scope without freeing
## anything. Before this pin landed, Ruxen's drop elaboration
## still treated the caller's local as droppable; when a spawner
## fn returned before its spawned task ran, drop fired on the
## heap block and the next executor pump dereferenced freed
## memory (SIGSEGV / exit 139).
##
## What this proves end-to-end:
##   - A short-lived async fn `spawner` allocates a future, calls
##     `Task.spawn_raw(fut)`, and returns the handle. Drop
##     elaboration on `spawner`'s `fut` local must NOT emit a
##     free — the executor's queue still owns the pointer.
##   - `main` block_on's `spawner()`, receives the handle, then
##     pumps the queue until the spawned future completes.
##   - `TaskHandle.result(h)` returns the i64 payload (42).
##
## Without the drops.rs fix this fixture SIGSEGV's on the first
## `ruxen_executor_pump_tasks()` call after `spawner` returns —
## the executor walks the queue and follows a freed pointer.

class PayloadFuture
  remaining: Int
  payload: Int
  include Future
  type Output = Int

  def init(n: Int, p: Int)
    self.remaining = n
    self.payload = p
  end

  def var poll(cx: &var Context) -> Poll[Int]
    if self.remaining == 0
      Poll.Ready(self.payload)
    else
      self.remaining = self.remaining - 1
      let w = cx.waker
      w.wake_by_ref
      Poll.Pending
    end
  end
end

## Short-lived spawner: allocates the future and hands it off
## to the executor. Without the ownership-move fix, `fut` is
## drop-elaborated at scope exit and freed before any pump
## sees it. With the fix, `Task.spawn_raw` taints `fut` so the
## drop pass skips it.
async def spawner -> Int
  let fut = PayloadFuture.new(2, 42)
  Task.spawn_raw(fut)
end

def main
  let h = block_on(spawner())
  # At this point `spawner`'s stack frame is gone. The future
  # the executor's queue references must still be valid. Pump
  # until the task reports done, then read the payload.
  let var done = 0
  loop
    let _pumped = ruxen_executor_pump_tasks()
    if TaskHandle.is_done(h) == 1
      let r = TaskHandle.result(h)
      if r == 42
        puts "ok"
      else
        puts "fail"
      end
      done = 1
      break
    end
  end
end
